1
00:00:00,420 --> 00:00:02,900
Potter (off-screen): I want you
to manage my properties.

2
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:05,630
$300,000 a year.

3
00:00:06,790 --> 00:00:07,900
Starting Monday.

4
00:00:10,680 --> 00:00:13,800
George: Three...
$300,000 a year?

5
00:00:15,150 --> 00:00:17,300
Potter: You wouldn't mind living
in the nicest house in town.

6
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:21,450
Your wife in clothes
she didn't order off a screen.

7
00:00:22,490 --> 00:00:24,100
Real trips, two a year.

8
00:00:24,540 --> 00:00:26,600
You wouldn't mind that,
would you, George?

9
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:28,200
[George chuckles]

10
00:00:29,220 --> 00:00:30,870
George: Would I?

11
00:00:31,870 --> 00:00:34,400
You're not talking to somebody
else around here, are you?

12
00:00:34,690 --> 00:00:36,420
You know, this is me.
You remember me?

13
00:00:37,940 --> 00:00:39,200
George Bailey.

14
00:00:40,050 --> 00:00:41,400
Potter: Oh yes, George Bailey.

15
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:43,900
Whose ship has finally come in...

16
00:00:44,560 --> 00:00:47,000
if he has the sense to board it.

17
00:00:51,440 --> 00:00:52,800
George: Well, what happens to Bailey?

18
00:00:52,990 --> 00:00:55,000
Potter: Oh, confound it, man.

19
00:00:56,550 --> 00:00:57,950
Are you afraid of success?

20
00:00:58,530 --> 00:01:01,350
I'm offering you $300,000 a year
starting Monday.

21
00:01:02,120 --> 00:01:03,300
Yes or no?

22
00:01:03,750 --> 00:01:04,800
George: Hmm...

23
00:01:07,170 --> 00:01:08,700
Well, Mr. Potter, I...

24
00:01:09,580 --> 00:01:11,900
I know I ought to jump
at the chance, but...

25
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:13,400
I just...

26
00:01:15,640 --> 00:01:16,950
I wonder if it would be possible

27
00:01:17,460 --> 00:01:20,300
for you to give me 24 hours
to think it over?

28
00:01:20,660 --> 00:01:22,200
Potter: Sure, sure, sure.

29
00:01:23,380 --> 00:01:25,300
You go on home and talk
about it to your wife.

30
00:01:26,800 --> 00:01:28,300
George: I'd like to do that.

31
00:01:28,950 --> 00:01:31,450
Potter: In the meantime,
I'll draw up the papers.

32
00:01:33,080 --> 00:01:34,200
George: All right, sir.

33
00:01:39,180 --> 00:01:40,350
Potter: Okay, George?

34
00:01:40,450 --> 00:01:42,300
George: Okay, Mr. Potter.

35
00:01:51,530 --> 00:01:52,700
No.

36
00:01:52,810 --> 00:01:54,700
No, no, no.
Now wait a minute here.

37
00:01:55,810 --> 00:01:57,300
I don't have to talk to anybody.

38
00:01:58,100 --> 00:02:00,550
I know right now,
and the answer is no.

39
00:02:01,760 --> 00:02:03,100
No! Damn it!

40
00:02:03,590 --> 00:02:04,700
You sit around here

41
00:02:05,170 --> 00:02:07,550
and you spin your little webs,

42
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:10,900
and you think the whole world revolves
around you and your money.

43
00:02:12,020 --> 00:02:13,700
Well, it doesn't, Mr. Potter.

44
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:16,250
In the whole vast
configuration of things,

45
00:02:16,730 --> 00:02:19,300
I'd say you were nothing
but a scurvy little spider.

46
00:02:20,330 --> 00:02:21,850
A small, sad spider

47
00:02:22,210 --> 00:02:23,800
in a very expensive web.

48
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:38,200
[door clicks shut]

